# Rust
**/target/
corpus/generate/out/

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# CI (hyper-pack-nuget.yml) arranges and packs these per-RID at pack time; regenerable
# locally via `cargo cdylib` (the csproj's runtimes/**/native/* wildcard item).
csharp/HyperTabular/runtimes/
# The same for the static libraries a Native AOT publish links in: staged by the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh at test and pack time, never committed.
csharp/HyperTabular/staticlibs/

# Gradle / Java
**/.gradle/
**/build/
# CI places each leg's native library here before `gradlew test`, and the Maven publish
# bundles every platform's at publish time; the local dev loop stages into
# build/generated-resources instead (already covered by **/build/ above), so anything here
# is regenerable via `cargo cdylib`.
java/src/main/resources/native/
# csharp/HyperTabular/build/ is NuGet's real, tracked build/{PackageId}.targets packaging
# convention, not a build output. It collides with **/build/ above, which would otherwise
# silently swallow anything new in it: the file would sit on disk, pack correctly in a
# local `dotnet pack`, and simply never exist in CI. Each directory level needs its own
# negation — git won't descend into an excluded directory to find a deeper !file
# re-inclusion — and gitignore rules apply in file order, so this must come after the rule
# it un-ignores. HyperCast carries the same block for the same reason.
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/net11.0/
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/net11.0/HyperTabular.targets
